          "date": "2026-10-30 17:40:51.000000000",
          "tz": -240
        },
        "subject": "LU-21078 build: make deb packages reproducible",
        "message": "LU-21078 build: make deb packages reproducible\n\nStarting with Debian 14 (\"forky\"), Debian requires packages to be\nreproducible, so that anyone can rebuild a package and verify that\nit matches the published binary\n(https://lists.debian.org/debian-devel-announce/2026/05/msg00001.html).\nLustre debs built from the same tree on the same machine did not\nmatch: each build produced files with different checksums.\n\nThere were three causes:\n\n- The changelog entry written by \"make debs\" and \"make dkms-debs\"\n  used the current time, and dpkg-buildpackage derives\n  SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH from it, so file mtimes in the packages\n  changed on every build. The module-assistant step runs outside\n  dpkg-buildpackage and never saw that value.\n- configure saves each kernel feature check in\n  kconftest.results/$RANDOM, and the dkms and lustre-source\n  packages copied these directories.\n- The lustre-source tarball recorded file mtimes, owners and\n  ordering.\n\nSet SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH to the HEAD commit time, export it so that\nevery packaging step uses it, and use it for the changelog date.\nSort the entries in the lustre-source tarball and normalize their\nowner and mtime. Exclude kconftest.dir and kconftest.results from\nthe rsync copies.\n\nSee https://wiki.debian.org/ReproducibleBuilds for background.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Manhong Dai <manhong.dai@netapp.com>\nSigned-off-by: Cory Spitz <Cory.Spitz@netapp.com>\nChange-Id: I7b9e101471c2fc46e84fc2695bb5f08279bea7ee\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
